.\" Distro-authored man page for the Fedora pidp8i package.
.\" Candidate for upstreaming to the PiDP-8/I project.
.TH PTP2TXT 1 "November 21, 2026" "PiDP-8/I" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ptp2txt, txt2ptp \- convert between paper-tape images and text
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ptp2txt
.RI [ file ...]
.br
.B txt2ptp
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ptp2txt
converts a PDP-8 paper-tape image (the
.I .pt
/
.I .ptp
formats used by PALGAIL/BARTGNO output and the OS/8 tools) into the
readable text form, and
.B txt2ptp
converts in the other direction, re-punching the leader, information
and parity blocks.
.PP
Both names are the same program: the direction is chosen by the name
it was invoked as. With no file arguments it acts as a stdin-to-stdout
filter; with file arguments it converts each one, writing the result
beside it with the corresponding extension. Unreadable files are
reported (
.IR "Open of input file ... failed" )
and skipped.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ ptp2txt add.pt              # dump a punched tape as text
$ txt2ptp notes.txt           # punch text back into a tape image
$ cat boot.pt | ptp2txt       # filter form
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR palbart (1),
.BR d8tape (1)
